From 6349f6f1f7ca6d3ae19a86b680769d5ca8968967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aditya Arnav <140049169+Hydra-Of-Malice@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:01:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(circuit-kit): rank layers by total node score with
 layer_fraction

circuit_info_from_node_scores keeps every layer holding any top-fraction
node. Top nodes are spread through a model, so a top-20% node set selected
30 of 36 layers on Tiny Aya, and a circuit-restricted edit restricted little.

Add layer_fraction to circuit_info_from_node_scores,
load_circuit_info_from_file and get_circuit_info. It selects the top
fraction of layers by total absolute node score (new layer_mass and
top_layers), and top_fraction then picks among the nodes in those layers.

The argument is opt-in, so existing results do not change. When it is set
on a file that has node_scores, it replaces the safety_units and
layer_suggestions keys, because CircuitKIT 0.2 writes those with the
unranked selection and they would otherwise win.

